web/.impeccable/

# env files (secrets) — never commit.
# `.env.local` matters as much as `.env` here: `web/e2e/README.md` tells you to
# put a throwaway AUTH_SECRET in `web/.env.local`, and Next's `loadEnvConfig`
# reads it — but `*/.env` does not match it, so it was untracked-by-luck only.
# Holding AUTH_SECRET is equivalent to being able to sign in as anyone.
.env
.env.local
*/.env
*/.env.local
.env.*.local

